Decomposition identity CONFIRMED at every (n,gamma) point tested: the
mismatch between the LHS gap S_n'-G_n-1/(2*gamma) and the RHS crossover
sum is, at every point, well within the analytically-predicted bound on
the neglected pieces (T_prof tail beyond the summation cutoff, plus the
Poisson k>=1 remainder) -- both provably exponentially small in n per
scripts 02/03. This is genuine numerical confirmation of script 02's
algebra applied to the TRUE discrete sum, not merely the T_prof proxy
tested in script 03.

